From: Rune Lillesveen <futhark@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:46:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [M159] Fix concurrent Oilpan marking races in CSSSelectorList

Original change's description:
> Fix concurrent Oilpan marking races in CSSSelectorList
>
> Oilpan marks an object as fully constructed when MakeGarbageCollected()
> finishes, which orders constructor writes before a concurrent marker
> calls Trace(). Populate first_selector_ inside CSSSelectorList
> constructors instead of after MakeGarbageCollected() returns, and read
> the list terminator via IsLastInSelectorListForOilpan() in Trace() so
> concurrent marking does not race with either list initialization or
> main-thread selector bucketing.
>
> Bug: 586990502
>
> Change-Id: Ie32c059cf0e3e271c3de0f8cc7f0933a05f3bfc3
